-- title:
--   The round-six parameters in `ℕ` form (`r6_axis_nat`)
-- statement:
--   The round-six parameters in `ℕ` form: `0 < s < t`, `2 ≤ α`, `3 s ≤ α² (t - s)` (`α²θ ≥ 3`),
--   `6 d ≤ s`, `48 d² ≤ α² ≤ p`, `p < 48 d (α+1)²`, `3072 ≤ b'`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegR6`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.r6_axis_nat (P : Prm) (hP : P.Ok) : ∃ n₁ : ℕ, ∀ n, n₁ ≤ n → ∀ src : ℕ → ℕ,
--       SrcOK6 P n src → ∀ j < dP6 P n,
--         0 < src j ∧ src j < tF6 P n j ∧ 2 ≤ αN6 P n ∧
--         3 * src j ≤ αN6 P n ^ 2 * (tF6 P n j - src j) ∧ 6 * dP6 P n ≤ src j ∧
--         48 * dP6 P n ^ 2 ≤ αN6 P n ^ 2 ∧ αN6 P n ^ 2 ≤ pP6 P n ∧
--         pP6 P n < 48 * dP6 P n * (αN6 P n + 1) ^ 2 ∧ 3072 ≤ b'P6 P n ∧ 1 ≤ dP6 P n
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Segmented inverse (S2): the round-six regime
--
--   `r6_axis_hyps`: for every `P` with `P.Ok` there is `n₁` such that for `n ≥ n₁`, every admissible
--   source list (`SrcOK6`) and every axis `j < d`, the hypotheses of the segmented-inverse theorems
--   hold with `s = src j`, `t = tF6 j`, `α = αN6`:
--   `0 < s < t`, `2 ≤ α` and `α²θ = xθ s t α ≥ 3`.
--
--   Proof: `SrcOK6` forces the window `w_j = ⌊t/(8d²)⌋ ≥ 1`, so `t - s ≥ w_j ≥ t/(16d²)`; and
--   `α² ≥ 48 d²` as soon as `b' = b^{1+x} ≥ 3072 d³`, which holds for large `b` because
--   `d ≤ b^ε` and `3ε < 1 + x` (`Prm.Ok.three_eps`).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Part of the Lean formalization of the round-six κ-improvement (integer-multiplication-kappa campaign, target `IntMul.Kappa.jain_round6_framework`). The statement is copied verbatim from the Lean development; the platform node carries the same declaration name. Definitions it mentions live in the `IntMul_Kappa_R6_Defs*` bundles (on top of the published κ bundles `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs*`).
